Chatterbox TTS (Resemble AI) — MIT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

self.speak's second (voice-cloning) engine is Resemble AI's Chatterbox
(https://github.com/resemble-ai/chatterbox), used UNMODIFIED as a pip dependency
(`chatterbox-tts`) installed into an isolated second venv (/app/.venv-chatterbox),
plus the `ResembleAI/chatterbox` model weights pulled at runtime from the Hugging
Face Hub. Both the `chatterbox-tts` package and the Chatterbox model weights are
licensed MIT by Resemble AI. Like the Kokoro dependencies above, Chatterbox is an
unmodified third-party component used as-is; only self.speak's own worker/adapter
code (api/src/chatterbox_worker/) is original and licensed GPLv3 with the rest of
this repo. MIT is one-way compatible with GPLv3, so the combined work is GPLv3
while Chatterbox's MIT terms are honored for the unmodified upstream component.
self.speak is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to Resemble AI.
